Done. All five rule modules implemented + tested.

**changed:** `crates/core/src/text/{tidy,fillers,corrections,spoken,lists}.rs` (only my files; `mod.rs` untouched)

**Design (short):**
- `tidy` — space collapse, line trim, space-before-punct, redundant-comma collapse, sentence capitalization, lone `i`→`I`; never adds final period. Shared normalizer the other four rules end with (so no double spaces / leading commas can survive, and `tidy` is already the last pipeline stage → idempotent no-op).
- `fillers` — word-scan; filler removed only when bounded by punctuation/text edges, with an adjacent comma (or sentence period) folded in; ranges merged then deleted; stutter collapse loops over the 13-word list (`that that`/`had had` kept).
- `corrections` — sentence-tagged word scan; marker → R (rest of sentence); cut from R[0]'s backward occurrence else drop last `len(R)` words; `scratch/delete/never mind that` retract the preceding sentence, or the clause before the marker's last delimiter. `marker` with no preceding word in the sentence is ignored (covers `No wait is too long.` / `I mean it when I say…`). Marker list uses `make that` (not `actually make that`) — that is what makes `Buy milk, actually make that oat milk.` → `Buy oat milk.`
- `spoken` — phrase + glued spaces/comma-period replaced by `\n`/`\n\n`; a comma *before* the phrase is kept (`Hi team,\n\n…`).
- `lists` — ordinals + `number one…ten`; run must start at 1 and count up, extending markers need a comma/`and` before them (kills `a second opinion`); intro → `:` line, items cleaned/capitalized via tidy's `N. ` prefix, later sentence kept as `\n\n` paragraph.

